  "wire_is_a_floor": "RETIRED Tue 27 Oct 2026 by Q129(a) -- it is NOT a lower bound, and this key's name is historical. The between-cell capacitance here is the global-route Steiner estimate, and that estimate is not coupling-free: the ORFS asap7 setRC.tcl hands it 0.1658 fF/um for a signal wire, a layer's TOTAL capacitance at nominal spacing with the neighbour coupling already bundled in and grounded. Detailed routing now closes and OpenRCX extraction puts the estimate 20-23% ABOVE the extraction at Miller k=1 (14,427 against 12,006 fF on the mixed netlist, +20.2%; 15,533 against 12,605 on this kept one, +23.2%), with coupling 58% of the k=1 wire capacitance each driver sees. So the wire share here is a CEILING and the transistor share a FLOOR: scaling this section's own split by that measured ratio moves the signal-net transistor share from 21.7% to about 23.4% and the clock-net one from 17.1% to about 20.2% -- a scaling, not a re-measurement. See docs/reports/data/2026-10-27-q129-routed-netlist/."
