   "verdict": "the minimum is real at both rails: 300 ps at 0.517 V and 50 ps at 0.700 V. Over the whole 1 ps - 2 ns range the spread is 7.5% of a cycle at 0.517 V against 59% at 0.700 V, so short circuit is the term that blows up at the higher rail and is worth a couple of percent at the minion's. This inverter's own output edge into this load is 23.4 ps (20-80%), where it sits 2.2% above its minimum.",
